<title>BRAZIL: BRAZIL'S REAL ENDS OFF 0.04 PCT IN CALM TRADING.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL'S REAL ENDS OFF 0.04 PCT IN CALM TRADING.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's real ended fell 0.04 percent to end at 1.0856 per dollar in calm trading in the commercial foreign exchange market Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the interbank floating rate market, the real closed off 0.02 percent at 1.0906 per greenback, while in the parallel market the real currency was flat at 1.135 per dollar.</p>
<p>((--Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485418))</p>
